Decode JSON string escapes, and escape a quote as a quote

Applies to: flutter-pi, tag release/1.1.1
            https://github.com/ardera/flutter-pi
            MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Hannes Winkler

flutter-pi's JSON parser never decodes string escapes. jsmn locates a
string's bytes and platch_decode_value_json hands them over as they are --
the "use zero-copy approach" comment -- so `{"text":"a\nb"}` arrives as four
characters: 'a', a backslash, an 'n', 'b'. The encoder then escapes that
backslash correctly on the way out, so the peer gets a literal backslash
where its newline was, and every round trip doubles it. In a text field that
turns a document's newlines into \n and then \\n, drifts the caret by one
per newline (flutter-pi's buffer is longer than the text whose offsets it is
given), and ends at TEXT_INPUT_MAX_CHARS.

This decodes the escapes in place. Decoding only shortens -- the shortest
escape is two bytes for one, a surrogate pair twelve for four -- so the
result fits over the token it came from and the zero-copy pointer stays
valid. \uXXXX is handled, including surrogate pairs; a lone surrogate
becomes U+FFFD rather than invalid UTF-8; an unrecognized escape is kept
verbatim rather than dropped.

Also: the encoder wrote a double quote as backslash-'t', turning every `"`
into a tab.

Carried by BrainFrame because the binary flutterpi_tool downloads is
unusable for text editing without it; see docs/appimage.md. Not yet
submitted upstream.

